{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And if you do not listen to Me.</b> That you do not study Torah. And it goes on counting seven transgressions, one above the other: first, ״לא תשמעו״ — you do not listen; second, ״ולא תעשו״ — and you do not do; since they do not study, they do not fulfill, so these are two. ואם בחקותי תמאסו — if you reject My statutes — these are three, because the reason of the statutes is not known and therefore they reject them. ואם את משפטי תגעל נפשכם — if your soul abhors My judgments — they reject the civil laws, such as the laws of robbery and forbidden relations, which the spirit of people desires and which are a great yoke upon the wicked; and to teach how severe it is for one who rejects the judgments of the Holy One, blessed be He, He began with them here in this passage and concluded the passage with them at the end of all the curses, as it says ״יען וביען במשפטי מאסו״ — because and inasmuch as they rejected My judgments — these are four. לבלתי עשות — so as not to do — it is not enough that they do not fulfill them, but they prevent others from fulfilling them, and these are five. את כל מצותי — all My commandments — from this it follows that he denies all the commandments, for it did not say 'all the commandments' but ״את כל מצותי״, and these are six. להפרכם את בריתי — to break My covenant — until he comes to deny the very root of faith, and these are seven. Thus you have learned that there are seven transgressions here, for one transgression drags in another: from the fact that a person does not study, he comes to the second, and from the second to the third, until he is brought to the seventh, to deny the very root."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:28:45.567815523Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}